  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment opportunities for families affected by Lima floods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is the direct continuation of project PER291 Emergency Response in Chosica, Lima (areas of Carapongo and Barba Blanca). The central goal of this new follow-up project is to support 40 homeless and/or affected families in areas on the outskirts of Lima (in the jurisdiction of the Diocese of Chosica) to restore their livelihoods following the 2017 El Nino disaster. Following an initial diagnosis study to determine their eligibility, families/individuals will be supported with training, technical assistance and a seed capital to reactivate their small businesses and livelihood opportunities. Monitoring and specialist advice will be provided by the project team to support the success and sustainability of the businesses beyond the life of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
